@meeting talk.pell
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 13 (FX17's word list): a small Wren talk, 19:00-19:40 on the auditorium stage (a ring of eight
// chairs, house dark, the stars behind, tea from the kettle). Day 78, Monday. Pell Okafor, Works. Not his mum's shop or the practical.
title: Every panel that sticks
from: Pell Okafor
gist: Pell's small talk on every panel aboard that sticks, and how to unstick it.
== lines
pell: Oi oi. Right, so. Is there food? There's food. Brilliant. Sit down, sit down.   [gesture]
pell: Tonight: every panel on the Wren that sticks, and why. Long list. Short talk.   [laugh]
pell: Deck 5, third panel from the lift. Sticks every damp week. Hit it here. Gently. Lovingly.
pell: Why? Old seal. Calder knows. Calder's always known. She's waiting to see if I fix it.
pell: Right, so, the real secret. Most things that stick just want a clean and some patience.
pell: Same as people, my mum says. Usually about me.   [laugh]
pell: Questions? Quick ones. There's a biscuit out there with my name on it.
? choice
* Why haven't you fixed it?   rel:pell+2 flavour:cheer mem:talk.pell.asked
  pell: Then what would I talk about? No, I'm doing it. Next week. Probably.   [laugh]
* Where do the good spanners hide?   rel:pell+2 flavour:practical mem:talk.pell.asked
  pell: Bottom drawer, behind the tape. That was a secret. It was. Past tense.   [laugh]
* (Just listen)
  pell: No questions. Fair. Biscuits it is, then.
pell: Cheers, everyone. Mind that panel.
